## Schema

### Required

- `name` (String) Tenant name. Must be unique on the parent system.

### Optional

- `allow_branding` (Boolean) Allow the tenant to customize colors and logo. Omit to leave the current value unchanged.
- `change_password` (Boolean) Require a password change on first login. Sent only when the tenant is created. VergeOS does not return it, so Terraform keeps the configured value. Changing a configured value replaces the tenant.
- `description` (String) Tenant description. Omit to leave an existing description unchanged.
- `expose_cloud_snapshots` (Boolean) Allow the tenant to request system cloud snapshots.
- `help_url` (String) Custom help URL. `default` uses the product default. A blank value disables the help link.
- `note` (String) Free-form note stored on the tenant.
- `oidc_application` (Number) OIDC application key for SSO.
- `password` (String, Sensitive) Password for the tenant admin user. Omit to leave the current password unchanged.
- `powerstate` (Boolean) Whether the tenant is powered on. Omit to leave the current power unchanged.
- `preferred_node` (Number) Host node used when `powerstate` changes to true. Changing it while the tenant is already on does not move the tenant.
- `theme_access` (String) Theme visibility: `specified`, `host_only`, `local_only`, or `both`.
- `url` (String) Optional URL recorded on the tenant.

### Read-Only

- `created` (Number) Creation time as a Unix timestamp.
- `creator` (String) Username that created the tenant.
- `id` (String) Tenant key assigned by VergeOS.
- `is_snapshot` (Boolean) Whether this tenant record is a snapshot.
- `isolate` (Boolean) Whether network isolation is enabled. This resource does not change isolation.
- `state` (String) Simplified tenant state from tenant status: `online`, `offline`, `warning`, or `error`.
- `status` (String) Tenant status string, such as `online`, `starting`, `stopping`, or `offline`.
- `ui_address` (String) IP address of the tenant UI. Empty until VergeOS assigns one.
- `ui_address_id` (Number) Key of the vnet address row that holds the tenant UI address.
- `uuid` (String) Tenant UUID assigned by VergeOS.
- `vnet` (Number) Key of the network VergeOS creates for the tenant.

## Import

Import is supported using the tenant key. `password` and `preferred_node` are not returned by VergeOS, so ignore them on import when they are set in configuration.

```shell
terraform import vergeio_tenant.example <id>
```
